<title>SINGAPORE: Stationery maker Nippecraft sinks into red.</title>
<headline>Stationery maker Nippecraft sinks into red.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	  (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		 (7.98)  vs   0.51</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)    (3.99)  vs   0.26</p>
<p>    Turnover		   64.66   vs  67.09</p>
<p>    Operating pretax	  4.35   vs   7.01</p>
<p>    Interest expense	  4.12   vs   2.73</p>
<p>    Exceptional item	 (6.83)  vs  (0.86)</p>
<p>    Pretax		     (9.15)  vs   0.55</p>
<p>    Tax			   1.20   vs   nil</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  (4.14)  vs  (0.58)</p>
<p>Note _ Nippecraft Ltd said the total loss for the year of S$12.1 million includes exceptional and extraordinary losses, related to restructuring and rationalisation. The company is now 64 percent owned by Asia Pulp &amp; Paper Co.</p>
<p>It said it expects its operating performance to improve in the current year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
